# The crok-relay Vercel project builds relay/ (its Root Directory), so a CLI deploy runs from here, the repository
# root, and uploads this folder as it is: the Vercel CLI does not read .gitignore. Upload relay/ alone, without its
# secrets and local state (the files relay/.gitignore keeps out of git). Directory rules have no trailing slash so
# that they match the folder itself, not only what is inside it.
/*
!/relay
relay/**/.env
relay/**/.env.*
relay/**/.convex
relay/**/.phone-sim*.json
relay/**/.vercel
relay/**/node_modules
relay/**/.next
relay/**/out
relay/**/*.tsbuildinfo
